\section{The level-six lattice}\label{sec:s6}

\begin{calculation}[Engel's fibre lattice]
For Engel's based rank-four fibre lattice $\Lambda$ with invariant alternating form $\xi$, fibre class $\delta$ and primitive fibre character $\psi$, in the convention $\iota_\delta\xi(v)=\xi(\delta,v)$: $\iota_\delta\xi=-6\psi$, so $\ker\psi=\delta^{\perp_\xi}$, $\Lambda_{\mathrm{red}}=\ker\psi/\Z\delta$ has rank two with a unimodular induced form; $\xi^\flat:\Lambda\to\Lambda^*$ has Smith invariants $1,1,6,6$ (Pfaffian $-6$, determinant $36$), $D_\xi=\operatorname{coker}\xi^\flat\cong(\Z/6)^2$, and the finite Heisenberg group of $D_\xi$ with primitive central character has an explicit irreducible six-dimensional representation. For $G(r,s;m,n)=\langle c,x_0,x_1\mid c\text{ central},\ x_0x_1=1,\ x_0^r=c^m,\ x_1^s=c^n\rangle$ and $D=rn+sm\ne0$: $G\cong\Z/d_1\oplus\Z/d_2$ with $d_1=\gcd(r,s,m,n)$, $d_1d_2=|D|$ (with a global-section integer $b$ the determinant is $rn+sm-rsb$). In Engel's $(3,4)$ fibration with $m=3\psi(a_0)$, $n=4\psi(a_1)$: $D=12\psi(a_0+a_1)=p$, and $|p|=1$ makes $\pi_1$ trivial and $d_2(12\psi)=p\,\omega$ an isomorphism.
