\subsection{Consequences for the existing paper families}
The local and ordered-duality papers can use the Takiff category as a genuinely noncommuting test and can use the relative bar theorem with its exact categorical hypotheses. The mixed-obstruction papers gain a nonzero mixed triple coefficient and a nonseparable example, rather than another vanishing forced by commuting factors. The QFT papers gain the affine current/Ward realization but not a universal bulk or Einstein identification.

The arithmetic papers gain a specific nonabelian curvature calculation and a rational local Frobenius comparison. These do not prove a positivity or zeta-spectrum theorem. The Hall, BPS, Igusa, and cyclic-sewing papers still require their actual geometric coproducts, orientations, pairings, and line-valued comparisons. The level-six geometry papers still require singular fillings and attachment maps. None of those unrelated geometric inputs is manufactured by the present four-state model.

The proposed integration is therefore surgical: preserve the valid earlier results, add the new explicit comparison where its hypotheses match, and do not import theorems across categories without a map. No original source file was overwritten in this work.
