\begin{calculation}[{Engel's fibre lattice}]
For Engel's based rank-four fibre lattice $\Lambda$ with invariant alternating form $\xi$, fibre class $\delta$ and primitive fibre character $\psi$, in the convention $\iota_\delta\xi(v)=\xi(\delta,v)$: $\iota_\delta\xi=-6\psi$, so $\ker\psi=\delta^{\perp_\xi}$, $\Lambda_{\mathrm{red}}=\ker\psi/\Z\delta$ has rank two with a unimodular induced form; $\xi^\flat:\Lambda\to\Lambda^*$ has Smith invariants $1,1,6,6$ (Pfaffian $-6$, determinant $36$), $D_\xi=\operatorname{coker}\xi^\flat\cong(\Z/6)^2$, and the finite Heisenberg group of $D_\xi$ with primitive central character has an explicit irreducible six-dimensional representation. For $G(r,s;m,n)=\langle c,x_0,x_1\mid c\text{ central},\ x_0x_1=1,\ x_0^r=c^m,\ x_1^s=c^n\rangle$ and $D=rn+sm\ne0$: $G\cong\Z/d_1\oplus\Z/d_2$ with $d_1=\gcd(r,s,m,n)$, $d_1d_2=|D|$ (with a global-section integer $b$ the determinant is $rn+sm-rsb$). In Engel's $(3,4)$ fibration with $a_0\in\tfrac13\Lambda^{T_0}$, $a_1\in\tfrac14\Lambda^{T_1}$, $m=\psi(3a_0)$, $n=\psi(4a_1)$: $D=12\psi(a_0+a_1)=4m+3n=p$ and $\pi_1(Y(u))\cong\Z/|p|$; under the hypothesis $|p|=1$ of Engel's integral computation, $H^0(\mathbb P^1,R^1f_*\Z)=12\Z\psi$ and $d_2^{0,1}(12\psi)=p\,\omega$, an isomorphism (Theorem~\ref{thm:P5-engel}(4)).
