\begin{abstract}
An alternating rank-four integral lattice with elementary divisors $(1,6)$
has discriminant group $(\mathbb Z/6\mathbb Z)^2$.  We construct its perfect
discriminant pairing, an explicit finite Heisenberg group, and a
six-dimensional irreducible representation with faithful central character.
The calculation is purely arithmetic.  Its possible relation to a compact
complex threefold diffeomorphic to $S^6$ is stated only conditionally; neither
the existence of such a threefold nor a geometric origin for the lattice is
assumed.
\end{abstract}

