\section{A nonduplicating paper architecture}
The following is an editorial and mathematical decomposition, not a claim that every indicated volume is completed by this response. The canonical newly written material is the present book. Focused reading copies are labelled excerpts and preserve its numbering.

\paragraph{Core 0: relative operations and reconstruction.}
Factor out the carrier definitions, three bars, units and augmentations, filtered limits, divided-power normal resolution, higher module operations, tensor laws, and the rule that comparisons must preserve operations. Chapters~1--2 and the formal-group transport part of Chapter~\ref{ch:monodromy} supply proved components. The common core should not repeatedly reproduce the Igusa abstract or import a global equivalence from its intended applications.

\paragraph{Volume I: ordered and singular chiral geometry.}
This volume owns the geometric coefficient categories, collision extensions, the distinction between the two associative directions, and the three bar constructions. It may use the full operation-preserving normal reconstruction and logarithmic torus of Chapters~\ref{ch:normal} and \ref{ch:geometry}. A general singular ordered-chiral bar comparison still needs its own objects, maps, completion and descent proof. The classical chiral equivalence of Francis--Gaitsgory \cite{FG} is background in its actual category, not evidence for every newly proposed associative enhancement.

\paragraph{Volume II: local quantum fields and mixed holomorphic--topological systems.}
This volume owns the actual current envelopes, every state--field operation, scalar derived reconstruction, pre-Lie obstructions, higher normal actions, and mixed deformation problem. Chapters~\ref{ch:currents}, \ref{ch:geometry} and \ref{ch:physics} supply a tightly connected local family. Bulk centres, boundary endomorphisms, bar duals and traces retain different types. A global bulk-boundary comparison is not inferred from a shared Hilbert series.

\paragraph{Volume III: Calabi--Yau, Hall, and quantum-group realizations.}
This volume owns the geometric extension correspondences, orientation data, actual Hall multiplication, primitive and enveloping comparison maps, braided coproducts, quantum doubles and their completion. Chapter~\ref{ch:hall} supplies recognition tests and finite-window repairs. The explicit associative-action envelope retained in \cite{SourceAssociative} is a useful finite algebraic example, not a constructed compact Calabi--Yau Hall category.

\paragraph{Volume IV: integral and arithmetic reconstruction.}
This proposed functional slot owns the integral coefficient models, full Hasse translations, multiplicative monodromy, covers, restricted centres, Bockstein lifts and torsion. Chapters~\ref{ch:monodromy}--\ref{ch:integral} provide proved results. This is a proposed reorganization; it is not an assertion that the repository currently named vol4 already has this content or title. Arithmetic zeta realization and Weil positivity remain separate analytical obligations rather than automatic endpoints of the local modular calculation.

\paragraph{Companions with independent interfaces.}
The Igusa companion should retain the exact automorphic normalization and distinguish the formal root algebra from compact realization. The mixed-string companion should identify its actual open and closed carriers, cyclic structures and sewing maps. The gravity companion should begin with a proved sector such as Theorem~\ref{thm:classical-gravity} before making a quantum identification. The Deninger/Weil, arithmetic configuration/sieve, and S6 companions have their own inputs and proof obligations. They belong to the landscape without being forced to become synonyms for the same local construction.

